# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AlphaCode runs in the browser — there is no application server to configure.
#
# The ONLY environment variables that matter are the two OAuth ones, and they
# belong in your host's dashboard (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify / Vercel),
# never in the repo and never in the client bundle.
#
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_ID       from https://github.com/settings/developers → New OAuth App
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET   same page (keep it secret; it is only used by the function)
#
# Callback URL to register in the GitHub OAuth app:
#   https://<your-site-domain>/api/oauth/github/callback
#
# Without these, everything still works except "publish to your GitHub":
# instant previews, the harness, the shell, SQLite, files, exports.
#
# Model keys (Kilo / OpenCode / OpenRouter / Google / any BYOK) are entered by
# each user in Settings → Providers and stored in their own browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: pin the OAuth scope (default public_repo; use "repo" for private repos)
ALPHACODE_GITHUB_SCOPE=public_repo

# ── npm edge cache (optional, Cloudflare only) ──────────────────────────────
# The /api/npm function resolves dependency graphs once and caches the plan in
# KV, so the next install of the same packages is a single request. Create it:
#   npx wrangler kv namespace create NPM_CACHE
# then bind it as NPM_CACHE in Pages → Settings → Functions → KV namespace
# bindings (or uncomment kv_namespaces in wrangler.jsonc).
# Without it everything still works: the edge falls back to Cloudflare's
# per-colo cache and the browser falls back to resolving against the registry.

# ── MCP relay (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Some MCP servers do not send CORS headers, so a browser cannot call them.
# List the hosts you are willing to relay for; /api/mcp forwards to those only.
# MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=mcp.example.com,api.linear.app

# ── C/C++ (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiling C/C++ in the tab needs a clang+lld+sysroot bundle (~60 MB). Point
# this at a service you run that accepts {language, source, files} and returns
# a wasm32-wasi module. WASI binaries run here with no setup at all.
# ALPHACODE_CC_ENDPOINT=

# Optional: build-time knob, used by the Pages build to label the deployment
ALPHACODE_VERSION=3.0.0
